# GEO CAM Edge — appliance configuration (EnvironmentFile for systemd).
#
# Installed to /etc/geocam-edge/geocam-edge.env on first install and never
# overwritten by later installs/updates. Contains NO secrets:
# GEOCAM_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN is deliberately not settable here — the `enroll`
# CLI subcommand reads it from stdin or a one-shot environment variable at
# enrollment time only (see cmd/geocam-edge/main.go resolveEnrollmentToken),
# never from a file that would leave it sitting on disk in plaintext.
#
# Every variable below is read directly by internal/config.Load(); defaults
# and validation ranges shown are the actual values in that code, not
# aspirational ones. Uncomment a line to override its default.

# --- Core -------------------------------------------------------------
# GEOCAM_SAAS_URL=https://your-tenant.example.com
# GEOCAM_EDGE_ID=                       # normally left unset: generated once and persisted to
                                         # $GEOCAM_DATA_DIR/identity.json on first run
# GEOCAM_PROCESSING_MODE=cloud          # cloud|hybrid|edge — default: cloud.
                                         # HONESTY NOTE: only "cloud" has a working implementation
                                         # today. "hybrid" and "edge" are accepted by config parsing
                                         # (see internal/config/mode.go) but implement no functional
                                         # difference yet — do not select them in production.
# GEOCAM_LOG_LEVEL=info                 # debug|info|warn|error — default: info. Logs go to
                                         # stdout only (journald captures them); there is no
                                         # separate file-logging path to configure.
# GEOCAM_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/geocam-edge  # identity.json, credentials.json, offline buffer.
                                         # NEVER delete this directory to "reset" the appliance —
                                         # see docs/deployment/appliance.md.
# GEOCAM_HEALTH_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8091     # local-only health HTTP surface (/healthz /readyz /status)

# --- SaaS transport -----------------------------------------------------
# GEOCAM_SAAS_TIMEOUT=10s                #
# GEOCAM_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=false       # allow http:// (not https://) SaaS URLs — dev only
# GEOCAM_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL=30s          # bounds: 5s-5m

# --- LAN discovery (ONVIF/WS-Discovery) ---------------------------------
# GEOCAM_DISCOVERY_ENABLED=true
# GEOCAM_DISCOVERY_INTERVAL=5m           # bounds: 1m-24h
# GEOCAM_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT=4s            # bounds: 1s-30s
# GEOCAM_DISCOVERY_INTERFACES=           # comma-separated; default: auto-detect private interfaces

# --- Camera connectivity / RTSP -----------------------------------------
# GEOCAM_CONNECTIVITY_ENABLED=true
# GEOCAM_STREAM_ROLE=sub                 # sub|main — default: sub
# GEOCAM_STREAM_TIMEOUT=5s               # bounds: 1s-60s

# --- Video pipeline (ffmpeg subprocess) ---------------------------------
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_PIPELINE_ENABLED=false    # default OFF
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_TARGET_FPS=5              # bounds: 0.1-30
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_OUTPUT_WIDTH=640          # must be 0 (disabled, paired with height=0) or even, <=1920
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_OUTPUT_HEIGHT=360         # must be 0 (disabled, paired with width=0) or even, <=1080
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_RINGBUFFER_SIZE=30        # bounds: 1-300
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_QUEUE_DEPTH=64            # bounds: 4-512
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_DECODE_QUEUE_DEPTH=4      # bounds: 1-16
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_MAX_CONCURRENT_PIPELINES=4 # bounds: 1-16
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg        # When this package ships a static ffmpeg, install.sh
                                          # already points the service at it deterministically
                                          # (/opt/geocam-edge/current/ffmpeg) via the systemd unit —
                                          # no need to set this for that case. Uncomment only to
                                          # override with a different ffmpeg binary.
# GEOCAM_VIDEO_DECODE_TIMEOUT=10s        # bounds: 1s-60s

# --- Cloud offline buffer -------------------------------------------------
# These have NO production default in the code (see internal/config.go
# comments on CloudBufferMaxBytes/CloudBufferMaxFrames): buffering only
# activates once BOTH are set to a positive value. Leaving them unset keeps
# the pre-buffer behavior (drop frames on a failed Cloud push). This file
# intentionally does not suggest numbers — that policy decision is still
# open upstream in the code, not something this appliance packaging should
# invent.
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_BUFFER_MAX_BYTES=
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_BUFFER_MAX_FRAMES=
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_BUFFER_MAX_AGE=0          # 0 = no age-based eviction (safe default, unlike the two above)

# --- Cloud bandwidth control ----------------------------------------------
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_JPEG_QUALITY=85           # bounds: 1-100
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_MAX_BYTES_PER_SEC=0       # 0 = unlimited (default) — production value is an open
                                          # decision, not invented here
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_BURST_BYTES=0             # 0 = unlimited (default) — same as above
# GEOCAM_CLOUD_MAX_FPS=0                 # 0 = unlimited (default) — same as above
